      "id": "write-flash-resize-retains-old-devm-buffer-conditionally",
      "category": "lifetime",
      "severity": "CONDITIONAL_OLD_DEVM_ALLOCATION_CAN_REMAIN_UNFREED_UNTIL_DEVICE_TEARDOWN",
      "disposition": "STOCK_BEHAVIOR_DOCUMENTED; C_MIRROR_ERROR_STATE_ALIGNED_TO_GHIDRA",
      "details": "When a too-small existing buffer is present, the stock path first asks for the managed device. If that lookup returns NULL but the retry succeeds, it allocates a replacement without freeing old_data, so the old devm block remains registered until device teardown. If both lookups return NULL, stock clears the buffer pointer and size before returning -243; the caller cannot immediately free that old block through the context, though devres owns it until teardown. These are conditional stock lifetime behaviors; a live device-detach interleaving was not dynamically demonstrated. The source mirror previously retained the old pointer/size on the double-NULL branch, unlike Ghidra. The C mirror now clears both fields there, matching the exact stock control flow. The exact .S module is unchanged, so this source correction does not remove the runtime stock behavior.",
